.TH OCTA-AUDIO-CHECK 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-audio\-check \- prepare or exercise an ALSA PCM stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-audio-check\fR RATE capture|playback|prepare-capture|prepare-playback [PCM]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure S24_3LE interleaved hardware PCM at 44100, 48000, 96000 or 192000 Hz.
The default PCM is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0.
Capture/playback use 12/10 transport channels below 192 kHz and 4/4 at 192 kHz.
The requested period is RATE/100 frames with four periods per buffer.
.PP
Prepare modes configure and prepare without timed streaming.
Capture and playback exercise roughly one second of transfer; playback sends zeros.
The command may change hardware rate. Other PCM users must release the device.
Print preparation, transfer, timing and error information as JSON.
A successful transfer does not establish physical analog response or long-term stability.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
